{"version":"1","week":3,"level":"A1","pool":"training","fullTest":false,"yearExpansion":"year-expansion-69","sourceMaterialId":"expand-w03-read-2","source":{"schemaVersion":2,"kind":"derived-original","rights":"项目原创，AI辅助编写；模拟场景与数据","verification":"reviewed","method":"从本次新原创阅读派生的规则、原句词与不同情境输出；不改名复用旧源。","model":"deepseek-flash","contentHash":"327060596db0f40a00867c482a113c3300e688bc2a029ca4694871e7ca4d892e","contentHashFields":["title","instructions","passage","questions"],"yearExpansion":"year-expansion-69","practiceOnly":true,"independentAssessmentEligible":false,"independentTransferEligible":false,"sourceId":"expand-w03-read-2","parentContentHash":"4df18342c720e625b9c14e03f5d0a6b4f665489277091cf999f336a9f69787f9"},"questions":[{"id":"q1","type":"single","prompt":"We ___ a big table.","options":["have","has","are"],"answers":["have"],"explanation":"we 后用 have。","evidence":"We have a big table."},{"id":"q2","type":"single","prompt":"Ben ___ a small dog.","options":["have","has","are"],"answers":["has"],"explanation":"Ben 是第三人称单数，用 has。","evidence":"Ben has a small dog."},{"id":"q3","type":"single","prompt":"They ___ new members.","options":["are","is","am"],"answers":["are"],"explanation":"they 后用 are。","evidence":"They are new members."},{"id":"q4","type":"single","prompt":"___ name is Cara. (her / his / my)","options":["Her","His","My"],"answers":["Her"],"explanation":"Cara 是女性，用 her。","evidence":"Her name is Cara."},{"id":"q5","type":"single","prompt":"We ___ happy.","options":["are","is","am"],"answers":["are"],"explanation":"we 后用 are。","evidence":"We are happy."},{"id":"q6","type":"single","prompt":"___ pen is blue. (your / you / yours)","options":["Your","You","Yours"],"answers":["Your"],"explanation":"后面有名词 pen，用形容词性物主代词 your。","evidence":"You have a blue pen."},{"id":"q7","type":"single","prompt":"Are they happy? — Yes, ___.","options":["they are","they is","they am"],"answers":["they are"],"explanation":"they 的肯定回答用 they are。","evidence":"They are happy, too."},{"id":"q8","type":"single","prompt":"We ___ not sad.","options":["are","is","am"],"answers":["are"],"explanation":"we 的否定用 are not。","evidence":"We are happy."}],"id":"expand-w03-read-2-grammar","skill":"grammar","type":"grammar","estimatedMinutes":20,"title":"The Maple Street Club · 规则与新语境练习","instructions":"先阅读本组中文规则与原句，区分新结构和已学规则，再完成独立句子；同一材料再次出现属于巩固，保持原ID。","passage":"新规则：we（我们）和 they（他们/她们/它们）后面用 are。例如：We are happy. They are happy. 否定：We are not happy. They are not happy. 一般疑问：Are they happy? 回答：Yes, they are. / No, they are not. 形容词性物主代词：my（我的）、your（你的/你们的）、his（他的）、her（她的），后面必须接名词。例如：my bag, your pen, his dog, her cat。动词 have 表示“有”：I / you / we / they 用 have；he / she 用 has。例如：We have a table. Ben has a dog. 复习：I am, you are, he/she is（已学）。\n\nWe are happy. They are happy, too."}